Overlay patch 0044 (D-051; reference D-081 / Shipwright-ios 8f8e770 overlay 0062):
TOUCH DRAG-LOOK FOR FREE LOOK + TOUCH-C RIGHT-STICK MASK.

2S2H's Free Look camera (gEnhancements.Camera.FreeLook.Enable) had no touch
input: the touch overlay has no camera control. the Ship of Harkinian port answer is
DRAG-LOOK: a touch that lands on empty overlay space turns the free camera by
finger distance. The shell (app/ios/SohIosShell.m) owns the gesture; this
patch is the game side, __IOS__-gated (the desktop build is unchanged):

  1. padmgr.c PadMgr_UpdateInputs, port 1 (i == 0), once per pad tick (graph.c
     runs PadMgr_ThreadEntry once per game tick):
     a. SohIos_TouchLookTickDrain() moves the shell's accumulated drag into
        "this tick's delta" -- so a drag between two 20 Hz ticks is applied
        exactly once, and every reader in the tick sees the same value.
     b. THE TRAP THE TOUCH C-BUTTONS HAD ALREADY SPRUNG: they emit through SDL
        RIGHTX/RIGHTY (that is how they reach the C bits), and LUS's default
        mapping binds those SAME axes to the N64 right stick, which Free Look
        reads as a camera rate (and first-person RightStickEnabled reads as
        aim). So with Free Look on, every touch C press swung the camera. While
        SohIos_TouchCMaskActive() (a touch C held, and 0.25 s after) port 1's
        right stick is zeroed. The C BITS are untouched; physical pads never
        raise the mask (the overlay is hidden in controller mode).
        `cvar gSohIos.TouchCMask 0` is the A/B switch.

  2. FreeLook.cpp -- THE INJECTION POINT. 2S2H has no Mouse.cpp seam (the
     reference rode Mouse_HandleThirdPerson); Free Look reads
     input[0].cur.right_stick_x/y directly, x10 per tick, in two places:
     Camera_CanFreeLook's 15-unit engage threshold and Camera_FreeLook's
     yaw/pitch step. The touch delta is folded in at exactly those reads, with
     the Ship of Harkinian port sign convention (yaw: -stick*10 - touchX; pitch:
     stick*10 - touchY), so 2S2H's own RightStick.CameraSensitivity.X/Y, its
     invert options / Mirrored World and the MaxPitch/MinPitch clamp all apply
     on top, unchanged.
     Instruments for the console bridge's `look`: the free camera's yaw/pitch
     and a Camera_FreeLook tick count, a rate-limited shell log line when a
     touch delta reached the camera, and SohIos_CamYawPitch (the ACTIVE
     camera's eye->at yaw/pitch, Free Look engaged or not -- how the sim round
     proves a touch C press no longer swings it).

Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0043 applied and 0044 not applied.


